<!--
    kuna-varargsave: an x86-64 System V variadic function opens with the
    register-save prologue that implements va_start: the general argument
    registers past the named ones stored to the save area, then
    `test %al,%al; je; movaps %xmm0..%xmm7` into it.  It printed as an
    `if (al) { ... }` the source does not have, with every xmm and every
    general argument register as a parameter.
    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "own-input-prototype-recovery" (folded right after
    the first heritage pass, p4_calls/kuna_varargsave.rs).
    P0 assertion: `option varargsave on|off` (default on).
    Chunk 0x100000: gcc 11.4 -O2 -fno-inline -fcf-protection=none
    -fno-stack-protector -c, the two calls to vsink patched to its address:
      int vsink(int tag, const char *fmt, va_list ap) { return tag + fmt[0]; }
      int report(int tag, const char *fmt, ...)    hands its va_list on
      int scaled(double k, const char *fmt, ...)   the same, xmm0 is named
      double firstd(int n, ...)    va_arg(ap, double) once: gcc reads the
                                   saved xmm0 slot directly
      double dsum(int n, ...)      va_arg(ap, double) in a loop: indexes the
                                   save area through a register
    #1-#3 prove the fold (report and scaled print `...` after their named
    parameters, and pass those on); #4-#5 are the refused controls (a body
    that reads its own save area keeps the stores); #6-#7 prove the bug with
    the option off (fourteen parameters and the `if (v1)` block).
    The script pins `option dedupitetail on`: the default `latch` joins a loop
    latch gcc duplicated here, which changes the shape these asserts pin.
-->
